<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany blames Russia for Leipzig airport drone attack, orders Russian consulate closed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f303657f98dc811fbc6a7b0dea93f19a0256d6b71f5970ca99ef5ff09bdd094e</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed--4237b34f641e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed" /><summary type="html">Germany's government on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport on 4 August using an explosive-laden drone, and announced that it would shut down a Russian consulate among other measures against Moscow. French ​President Emmanuel Macron ​said he supported the ​adoption ‌of ⁠new European sanctions ‌against Russia after the attempted drone attack.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the new UK PM's agenda as he faces lawmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c63a1a02c42074197b9eedb6a9e21662c6ce70d182a4342e57c4848d8e4c2e8</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers--7159b8695669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers" /><summary type="html">Since taking office on July 20, Burnham has traveled around the country promising to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of his predecessor Keir Starmer. Now, it's time for him to face lawmakers for the first time since he has taken office after an unusually long time without having to do so due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us what to know from his speech.</summary></entry><entry><title>Replay: UK PM Andy Burnham faces lawmakers for first time since taking office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8a000ae8829102ea4f976e5f24b03b8ce4d5ea6268bbc850adc2214b5f1b84</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office--b2983eb40ac0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">Rewatch UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's first speech to parliament since taking office six weeks prior.</summary></entry><entry><title>After 'unprecedented honeymoon', UK PM faces lawmakers for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82c4bb37a70692a3ec829330a908f6ddff93e7fb65835278fdaa5323368f44a4</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time--5c153c598613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on September 1 for the first time since becoming UK leader six weeks ago. This comes as the wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy and ease the cost of living. Andy Burnham has enjoyed quite a long time without facing lawmakers due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 12 killed and over a dozen injured in Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f69165273b81801b118a1ac8b95aa96c3a95ef246dd515b46bd468c7cec9e59</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d546607aa696.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured many more in Kyiv and the surrounding region early on September 1, authorities said, marking the sixth straight day of intense strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Those injured three children, just as Ukrainian pupils return to school. In a new tactic, Moscow has sent swarms of new jet-powered drones to ⁠plague Kyiv and nearby areas day and night, killing residents and damaging homes and warehouses.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's G20 US invitation severely criticised by European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4f45c22f6d780db5f0ec2ebda6858b1c7ec9fe8559b8f5bdd906ced27b4e98f</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:48:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries--bc062679808d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries" /><summary type="html">Finance ministers and central bank governors from the group of 20 major economies are meeting for two days in Asheville, North Carolina. With the United States holding the rotating G20 presidency, Washington is trying to rally partners towards greater economic pressure on Iran and find ways to boost growth. But an unexpected attendee drew fierce criticism.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hopes for bolstered support as EU defence ministers meet in Dublin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a618ffffcd901d7e2cd57099e78fddde54d47e024ade46a92d9109eb801e6de5</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:34:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin--524abd2c9af0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin" /><summary type="html">EU defence ministers grapple with bolstering Ukraine's air defences, as worries grow over Russia's campaign to destabilise Kyiv's European backers. This comes as Moscow is taking advantage of Kyiv running low on US-built air defence missiles to intensify its attacks on the country. EU ministers are also expected to discuss Russia's hybrid war against Ukraine's European allies. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK needs 'substantial change', says PM Andy Burnham in maiden parliament speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff7d7a6f256ad3d28385a2e99457743260d2461b00dd9365fc3d8f3f6339e56</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:21:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office--eb38aa025937.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham said the UK needed "substantial change" at his maiden speech in the House of Commons on Tuesday. Burnham has promised to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of predecessor Keir Starmer, who announced Tuesday that he would resign his seat in Parliament after 11 years.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Massive' Russian missile, drone attacks on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58b7d03e39c6f2e477512e4fc273b47f82ca017a9574f06cac66dca1f6b12d3a</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv--2741b6e31ce0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured several more in Kyiv early on Tuesday, authorities said, in the sixth consecutive day of strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Russia, which began its full-scale invasion of its smaller neighbour in 2022, has escalated its air attacks in recent months, as gains made on the ground have slowed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia fired over 2,800 drones at Ukraine in August amid war tactic change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec635ee548df2136265470ce305e4463a71a05f5806203c5c435af96021e960</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change--64c40c91d843.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change" /><summary type="html">Over the course of the month of August, Russia launched more than 2,800 jet-propelled drones at Ukraine, a type of drone that is harder to shoot down. That has come with a massive uptick in the number of drones used, considerind those now found on the frontline are quite a new model: Ukrainian authorities say they are pressed into service almost immediately after leaving the factory. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry looks at those new drones, and how Russia is using them to try and change the course of the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Kyiv and its region for sixth consecutive night of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1efa3912babea288686f0bedeaacbcabc83f0dde0536af79bb64ad0beeb0efd1</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:39:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks--4b2d5a3bbbf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">At least nine people have been killed and 14 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine overnight. Moscow targeted Kyiv and the wider region in the attack, hitting a railway depot in the Kyiv. Russia's defence ministry said it had also struck infrastructure in the Southern Odesa region. Russia has intensified strikes on the beleaguered Ukrainian cities in recent weeks disrupting the daily lives of millions of people and triggering up to a dozen air-raid alerts a day.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lake Annecy gun linked to unsolved 2012 murder of British family in French Alps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:127462655798b2ff5ca67ba132b7798222d69e50876376b70679f49e8bd6110b</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T08:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline--d65d925f5927.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline" /><summary type="html">French officials say a Luger pistol fished out from the bottom of Lake Annecy shows similarities to the weapon used in the notorious 2012 killings of a British-Iraqi family and a French cyclist in the nearby village of Chevaline, opening up a new lead in a case that has befuddled investigators for over a decade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: 'Safe days in Russian skies are over,' warns Zelensky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ec7e2d60fe9687bb5cd0aac09778d5b005685d2ff43f1cf997ad37cd79cdcd9</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:29:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv--abb7e72e6993.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Tuesday warned airlines, insurance firms and passengers that Russian airspace would be "completely unsafe" and filled with Ukrainian drones for the duration of the war. His address came after a night of relentless Russian bombardment in Ukraine, which killed at least a dozen people. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least eight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e271ed8a0cba6b4d6b248c4f3810617079e79296fdd016f5ce0036f82c52153</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T02:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four--dac5ac77b624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four" /><summary type="html">A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least eight people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU suspends Brazilian meat imports over antibiotic compliance concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df820bd69e486519e51ce3e68e570f420b3193fb7e0188c6241eac790b832137</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:30:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T00:14:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-eu-suspends-brazilian-meat-imports-over-antibiotic-compliance-concerns--05264d1e21dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-eu-suspends-brazilian-meat-imports-over-antibiotic-compliance-concerns" /><summary type="html">The European Union will suspend imports of Brazilian meat and other animal products from Thursday, citing concerns over Brazil’s compliance with EU rules on antibiotic use in livestock. The move affects poultry, beef, eggs and honey, with Brussels offering no timeline for when trade can resume.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron seals €4.3-bn French frigate deal in Sweden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd43b6a8bc55d28a05ff81fcdb3edd9b2bb77b5067f0d659b9def6a6ff1a3ad5</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T19:28:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-macron-seals-_4-3-bn-french-frigate-deal-in-sweden--14abac052a42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-macron-seals-%E2%82%AC4-3-bn-french-frigate-deal-in-sweden" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron on Monday oversaw the signing of a 4.3-billion-euro ($4.9 billon) deal for Sweden to buy four French frigates as France and Sweden seek to tighten cooperation against a backdrop of growing Russian threats. Sweden is racing to boost its defences after Russia invaded Ukraine in 2022, with the Nordic country becoming a NATO member two years later. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>As Icelanders say no to resuming EU talks, what issues weighed in the election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0712fb8672936f8d6ff0d141f55c11ae9665a5beb72483c875798c6164b940ce</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:26:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election--b151c9c282a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election" /><summary type="html">Iceland's voters rejected restarting negotiations to join the European Union in a referendum that pitted concerns about geopolitical stability against keeping national control of Iceland’s prized fisheries. Talks with the EU to join the bloc had begun after the 2008 financial crisis but had been ended by a Eurosceptic government. But why did Icelanders say no? FRANCE 24's Armen Georgian tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain blames Israel, Russia for spreading disinformation during Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3373c674d101ca02a454db5f272430526253324aa6c47eb9dc6dd9f9377a0ee4</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:24:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis--536350545613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said there were signs Russia and Israel had spread the disinformation over Spain's migration policy that triggered last month's rush of migrants into Ceuta, but no evidence of Moroccan ​involvement. Both Israel and Russia have denied their involvement. Over 72,000 migrants ‌irregularly crossed from Morocco into the tiny Spanish territory between July 30 and 31 ⁠in an unprecedented surge. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Northern Cyprus, families wait for news of passengers from sunk ferry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0035415474a79b121207207209f6bd9d4a65969b6e2de54fbbe75033f23a6e02</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry--efcd34c2b217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry" /><summary type="html">Seven people have died after a passenger boat capsized in Northern Cyprus. 267 people were on board and 23 are still missing. The boat capsized just a few miles off Kyrenia Port in northern Cyprus - a territory occupied by Turkey but not internationally recognised. The ferry has now completely sunk - and the company that operates it says it is "deeply saddened by the tragic accident". It says a hotline has been set up to provide passengers' relatives with information.</summary></entry><entry><title>France gears up for an election year defined by a fragmented left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5c803c026cbbbc1e0ed030fef35b11d5493b96b253149d905855f90d618db9b</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:49:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left--3c88d139e4b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left" /><summary type="html">It's back-to-school week for France, and its politicians are no exception. With a year set to be dominated by a crucial presidential election, both the left and the right wing are hoping to get candidates that will stand a chance against far-right leader Marine Le Pen, who is currently topping the polls. But for now, the political spectrum remains fragmented. So, who is running so far? FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France and Sweden look to boost European sovereignty through stronger defence ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0037509c89dd5434092745e0a4b298a7f05b875f8a7668e068bb1e457076a8</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:22:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties--88a1fe36fd43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is visiting Sweden on August 31. The aim of the trip is to strengthen the strategic partnership between the two countries. Boosting defence ties is expected to top the agenda, as the war in Ukraine continues and the threat from Russia persists. The newest member of NATO has also expressed interest in joining France's nuclear deterrence initiative.</summary></entry><entry><title>Police arrest Swiss man after deadly rave shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54a66edd77bc24c4d33b70bc6e7b6b61a8ab0beca671b16d0fd7381e907601b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:01:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting--3916a36cf6c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting" /><summary type="html">Swiss police on Monday said they had arrested a 43-year-old man on suspicion of having carried out a deadly shooting at a rave in the town of Aargau Sunday morning. The attack killed a 22-year-old Italian woman and wounded five other people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez says Israel and Russia spread disinformation on Ceuta migrant crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e86ea56f812a3e93805699ee56353c237d605c6eb8136061354e1be4617f428</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T08:20:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-israel-and-russia-spread-disinformation-on-ceuta-migrant-crisis--3f72af16ac9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-israel-and-russia-spread-disinformation-on-ceuta-migrant-crisis" /><summary type="html">Centre-left Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Monday alleged that social networks linked to Israel and Russia had spread disinformation about the July migrant crisis in the Spanish exclave of Ceuta. He said the alleged smear campaign, which he maintained had also been magnified by far-right networks, had been driven in part by Madrid's opposition to the wars in Ukraine and the Middle East.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's Arctic activity poses 'direct threat' to Russia, Lavrov warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b1062b8a994925332f0c12d6e593d18c4aaa5f72c74672d1b4562084e909ed1</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T02:40:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-nato-arctic-activity-direct-threat-russia-lavrov--055328c62902.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-nato-arctic-activity-direct-threat-russia-lavrov" /><summary type="html">Russia views NATO’s growing activity in the Arctic as a direct security threat, Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov said on Monday. NATO launched its Arctic Sentry mission in February to strengthen its presence in the region amid tensions with Moscow and US President Donald Trump’s push to acquire Greenland.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ferry capsizes and sinks off northern Cyprus, killing 8</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f771a9c31606f6a8cc1b6305735c5521d8c084eed730867584ace57da619e785</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:08:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus--feec88e2674e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus" /><summary type="html">At least eight people died when a ferry carrying more than 260 people capsized and sunk off the coast of northern Cyprus on Sunday, according to local authorities. The ship's captain and seven crew members were arrested, said the prime minister of the self-proclaimed Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (TRNC).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce93bb0676ca7f60d05c58c6f6b683669a1f8685de081588f2cdb7de10193104</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:30:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum--6c9761c1e20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum" /><summary type="html">Icelanders voted to reject reopening EU membership talks, official results showed Sunday, dealing a blow to the government's push to join the bloc and handing a win to those who argued the country's prized fishing waters were too important to risk. The results will disappoint Brussels, which had hoped to welcome the Nordic country as a new member.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman kills one at Swiss rave party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00053326d65d688f7d5a081839ea396034d305062d52618db70f3d90bee90f0d</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party--9d00787eff7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party" /><summary type="html">A large-scale police operation is underway in Switzerland after a shooting at a rave in the town of Aarau, 46 kilometres west of Zurich, left one person dead and five others injured. Swiss daily Blick reported that some attendees initially mistook the gunshots for fireworks, until someone shouted, “everyone down”. Police are appealing to potential witnesses who may have photos or videos of the incident to come forward and share them with investigators. France 24 correspondent John Zarocostas reports from Zurich.</summary></entry><entry><title>Manhunt under way after one killed, multiple injured at Swiss rave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daffbf08766c75ffb58c6750679af1a6294cd993db28c6c1e045d6d24be996ca</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:52:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland--affc514f1781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland" /><summary type="html">At least one person was killed and five others injured – some seriously – in a shooting at a rave in the northern Swiss city of Aarau, police and local media reported Sunday. A major police operation is underway at the scene, with authorities urging residents to stay away from the area.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Referendum on EU membership: An ‘existential question’ for Icelanders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d59ffd8737c4922045dbced5ff698eb960132a445841f4ee1ccccbd8ccd7a044</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders--be87b35411b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders" /><summary type="html">As Icelanders head to the polls on Saturday to vote in a referendum on whether the country should resume talks with the EU over membership, FRANCE 24 speaks to Eiríkur Bergmann, Professor of Politics at Bifröst University, for more insight into the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Warehouse hit by Russian attack stored munitions, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e2919de0c4e3aa47c6ac258563586350da0151d0f92099aa3fb0146cfde486</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:35:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says--67979b139afa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A depot that exploded in a Russian strike overnight was owned by the Ukrainian military and stored shells, drones, and other munitions, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Saturday. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry></feed>
